Q: How can I enforce copy elision? Why won&#39;t it work with a deleted copy constructor? A: <p>The OP's code is now valid since C++17. But GCC and Clang will only accept it when the option <code>std=c++17</code> is enabled.</p>
<p>Using the following minimum code as an example:</p>
<pre><code>class Uncopyable
{
public:
    // Should never be copied by value
    Uncopyable (const Uncopyable&amp;) = delete;
    Uncopyable&amp; operator= (const Uncopyable&amp;) = delete;

    Uncopyable() {}
};

int main(void)
{
    Uncopyable obj1;
    auto obj2 = Uncopyable();
}
</code></pre>
<p>When compiled with <code>std=c++14</code>, a compiler only accepts the declaration of <code>obj1</code>, but it rejects assignment to <code>obj2</code> as invalid. GCC shows the following errors:</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>g++ copyassignment.cpp -Wall -Wextra -O2 -std=c++14 -pedantic
</code></pre>
<p>Output:</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>copyassignment.cpp: In function ‘int main()’:
copyassignment.cpp:14:32: error: use of deleted function ‘Uncopyable::Uncopyable(const Uncopyable&amp;)’
   14 |         auto obj2 = Uncopyable();
      |                                ^
copyassignment.cpp:5:9: note: declared here
    5 |         Uncopyable (const Uncopyable&amp;) = delete;
      |         ^~~~~~~~~~
copyassignment.cpp:14:32: note: use ‘-fdiagnostics-all-candidates’ to display considered candidates
   14 |         auto obj2 = Uncopyable();
      |                                ^
copyassignment.cpp:14:14: warning: unused variable ‘obj2’ [-Wunused-variable]
   14 |         auto obj2 = Uncopyable();
      |              ^~~~
</code></pre>
<p>When compiled with <code>std=c++17</code>, compilers now accept both variables as legal, thanks to guaranteed copy elision:</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>copyassignment.cpp: In function ‘int main()’:
copyassignment.cpp:14:14: warning: variable ‘obj2’ set but not used [-Wunused-but-set-variable]
   14 |         auto obj2 = Uncopyable();
      |              ^~~~
</code></pre>
<p>Since copy elision is implicit, you can be relying on it without actually realizing the fact, and this incompatibility may come as a nasty surprise—as I accidentally discovered today. It shows the usefulness of deleted copy constructor as a compile-time assertion. Without deleting it, one may never notice this problem to begin with...</p>

Q: How to get list of DataTables metadata used in SSAS DSV? A: <p>you can use the following powershell script</p>
<pre><code>&lt;#
.SYNOPSIS
    Extracts Oracle table names from one or more SSAS XMLA script files.

.DESCRIPTION
    Searches XMLA files for Oracle table references in:
      - &lt;DbTableName&gt; tags
      - &lt;QueryDefinition&gt; SQL blocks (FROM / JOIN clauses)
      - &lt;TableID&gt; tags
      - &lt;![CDATA[...]]&gt; sections containing SQL
    Supports multiple files, wildcard paths, CSV/TSV output and source tracking.

.PARAMETER Files
    One or more XMLA file paths. Supports wildcards e.g. *.xmla

.PARAMETER Output
    Optional output file path. If omitted results print to console.

.PARAMETER Format
    Output format: list (default), csv, or tsv.

.PARAMETER WithSource
    Show which file each table was found in.

.EXAMPLE
    .\xmla_table_extractor.ps1 -Files cube.xmla

.EXAMPLE
    .\xmla_table_extractor.ps1 -Files *.xmla -Format csv -Output tables.csv

.EXAMPLE
    .\xmla_table_extractor.ps1 -Files cube1.xmla,cube2.xmla -WithSource

.EXAMPLE
    .\xmla_table_extractor.ps1 -Files *.xmla -Format csv -WithSource -Output all_tables.csv
#&gt;

[CmdletBinding()]
param(
    [Parameter(Mandatory=$true, Position=0)]
    [string[]] $Files,

    [Parameter(Mandatory=$false)]
    [string] $Output,

    [Parameter(Mandatory=$false)]
    [ValidateSet(&quot;list&quot;,&quot;csv&quot;,&quot;tsv&quot;)]
    [string] $Format = &quot;list&quot;,

    [Parameter(Mandatory=$false)]
    [switch] $WithSource
)

# ── SQL keywords to exclude as false positives ────────────────────────────────
$SQL_KEYWORDS = @(
    &quot;SELECT&quot;,&quot;WHERE&quot;,&quot;AND&quot;,&quot;OR&quot;,&quot;NOT&quot;,&quot;IN&quot;,&quot;ON&quot;,&quot;SET&quot;,&quot;AS&quot;,&quot;FROM&quot;,&quot;JOIN&quot;,
    &quot;INNER&quot;,&quot;OUTER&quot;,&quot;LEFT&quot;,&quot;RIGHT&quot;,&quot;FULL&quot;,&quot;CROSS&quot;,&quot;NATURAL&quot;,
    &quot;GROUP&quot;,&quot;ORDER&quot;,&quot;BY&quot;,&quot;HAVING&quot;,&quot;UNION&quot;,&quot;INTERSECT&quot;,&quot;EXCEPT&quot;,
    &quot;WITH&quot;,&quot;CASE&quot;,&quot;WHEN&quot;,&quot;THEN&quot;,&quot;ELSE&quot;,&quot;END&quot;,&quot;DISTINCT&quot;,
    &quot;COUNT&quot;,&quot;SUM&quot;,&quot;AVG&quot;,&quot;MIN&quot;,&quot;MAX&quot;,&quot;COALESCE&quot;,&quot;NVL&quot;,&quot;DECODE&quot;,
    &quot;DUAL&quot;,&quot;ROWNUM&quot;,&quot;SYSDATE&quot;,&quot;NULL&quot;,&quot;TRUE&quot;,&quot;FALSE&quot;,
    &quot;INTO&quot;,&quot;VALUES&quot;,&quot;UPDATE&quot;,&quot;DELETE&quot;,&quot;INSERT&quot;,&quot;CREATE&quot;,&quot;DROP&quot;,&quot;ALTER&quot;,
    &quot;TABLE&quot;,&quot;VIEW&quot;,&quot;INDEX&quot;,&quot;PROCEDURE&quot;,&quot;FUNCTION&quot;,&quot;TRIGGER&quot;,&quot;SEQUENCE&quot;
)

# Known schema-only names to skip
$KNOWN_SCHEMAS = @(&quot;DBO&quot;,&quot;SYS&quot;,&quot;SYSTEM&quot;,&quot;INFORMATION_SCHEMA&quot;)

# ── Strip SQL comments ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
function Remove-SqlComments {
    param([string]$Sql)
    # Remove block comments /* ... */
    $Sql = [regex]::Replace($Sql, '/\*.*?\*/', ' ', 'Singleline')
    # Remove line comments -- ...
    $Sql = [regex]::Replace($Sql, '--[^\n]*', ' ')
    return $Sql
}

# ── Extract tables from a SQL string ─────────────────────────────────────────
function Get-TablesFromSql {
    param([string]$Sql)

    $tables = [System.Collections.Generic.HashSet[string]]::new(
        [System.StringComparer]::OrdinalIgnoreCase)

    $Sql = Remove-SqlComments -Sql $Sql

    # Match: FROM/JOIN  [schema.]table  [alias]
    # Handles quoted and unquoted names
    $pattern = '(?:FROM|JOIN)\s+' +
               '(?:(?:&quot;([^&quot;]+)&quot;|([A-Z][A-Z0-9_$#]*))\.)?'+
               '(?:&quot;([^&quot;]+)&quot;|([A-Z][A-Z0-9_$#]{2,}))' +
               '(?:\s+(?:AS\s+)?[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*)?'

    $regex = [regex]::new($pattern, 'IgnoreCase')
    $matches = $regex.Matches($Sql)

    foreach ($m in $matches) {
        $schema = if ($m.Groups[1].Success) { $m.Groups[1].Value.ToUpper() }
                  elseif ($m.Groups[2].Success) { $m.Groups[2].Value.ToUpper() }
                  else { &quot;&quot; }

        $name   = if ($m.Groups[3].Success) { $m.Groups[3].Value.ToUpper() }
                  elseif ($m.Groups[4].Success) { $m.Groups[4].Value.ToUpper() }
                  else { &quot;&quot; }

        if (-not $name) { continue }
        if ($name.Length -lt 2) { continue }
        if ($SQL_KEYWORDS -contains $name) { continue }
        if ($schema -and ($SQL_KEYWORDS -contains $schema)) { continue }

        $full = if ($schema) { &quot;$schema.$name&quot; } else { $name }
        [void]$tables.Add($full)
    }

    return $tables
}

# ── Extract tables from one XMLA file content ─────────────────────────────────
function Get-TablesFromXmla {
    param([string]$Content)

    $tables = [System.Collections.Generic.HashSet[string]]::new(
        [System.StringComparer]::OrdinalIgnoreCase)

    # 1. &lt;DbTableName&gt;SCHEMA.TABLE&lt;/DbTableName&gt;
    $rx = [regex]::new('&lt;DbTableName[^&gt;]*&gt;([^&lt;]+)&lt;/DbTableName&gt;', 'IgnoreCase')
    foreach ($m in $rx.Matches($Content)) {
        $val = $m.Groups[1].Value.Trim().ToUpper()
        if ($val) { [void]$tables.Add($val) }
    }

    # 2. &lt;TableID&gt;TABLE&lt;/TableID&gt;
    $rx = [regex]::new('&lt;TableID[^&gt;]*&gt;([^&lt;]+)&lt;/TableID&gt;', 'IgnoreCase')
    foreach ($m in $rx.Matches($Content)) {
        $val = $m.Groups[1].Value.Trim().ToUpper()
        if ($val -and $val.Length -ge 3 -and ($SQL_KEYWORDS -notcontains $val)) {
            [void]$tables.Add($val)
        }
    }

    # 3. SQL inside &lt;QueryDefinition&gt; ... &lt;/QueryDefinition&gt;
    $rx = [regex]::new(
        '&lt;(?:msdata:)?QueryDefinition[^&gt;]*&gt;(.*?)&lt;/(?:msdata:)?QueryDefinition&gt;',
        'IgnoreCase,Singleline')
    foreach ($m in $rx.Matches($Content)) {
        $sql = $m.Groups[1].Value
        # Decode XML entities
        $sql = $sql -replace '&amp;amp;','&amp;' -replace '&amp;lt;','&lt;' -replace '&amp;gt;','&gt;'
        foreach ($t in (Get-TablesFromSql -Sql $sql)) {
            [void]$tables.Add($t)
        }
    }

    # 4. &lt;Query&gt; ... &lt;/Query&gt;  (partition / named query blocks)
    $rx = [regex]::new('&lt;Query[^&gt;]*&gt;(.*?)&lt;/Query&gt;', 'IgnoreCase,Singleline')
    foreach ($m in $rx.Matches($Content)) {
        $sql = $m.Groups[1].Value
        $sql = $sql -replace '&amp;amp;','&amp;' -replace '&amp;lt;','&lt;' -replace '&amp;gt;','&gt;'
        foreach ($t in (Get-TablesFromSql -Sql $sql)) {
            [void]$tables.Add($t)
        }
    }

    # 5. CDATA sections  &lt;![CDATA[ ... ]]&gt;
    $rx = [regex]::new('&lt;!\[CDATA\[(.*?)\]\]&gt;', 'Singleline')
    foreach ($m in $rx.Matches($Content)) {
        foreach ($t in (Get-TablesFromSql -Sql $m.Groups[1].Value)) {
            [void]$tables.Add($t)
        }
    }

    # ── Filter out noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    $filtered = [System.Collections.Generic.HashSet[string]]::new(
        [System.StringComparer]::OrdinalIgnoreCase)

    foreach ($t in $tables) {
        $name = if ($t -match '\.') { $t.Split('.')[-1] } else { $t }
        if ($name.Length -lt 3) { continue }
        if ($SQL_KEYWORDS -contains $name) { continue }
        if ($KNOWN_SCHEMAS -contains $t) { continue }
        [void]$filtered.Add($t)
    }

    return $filtered
}

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# MAIN
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Expand wildcards and collect file list
$resolvedFiles = @()
foreach ($pattern in $Files) {
    $found = Get-Item -Path $pattern -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
    if ($found) {
        $resolvedFiles += $found
    } else {
        Write-Warning &quot;File not found: $pattern&quot;
    }
}

if ($resolvedFiles.Count -eq 0) {
    Write-Error &quot;No XMLA files found.&quot;
    exit 1
}

# Process each file — store as table -&gt; [source files]
$allResults = [System.Collections.Generic.Dictionary[string,
    System.Collections.Generic.List[string]]]::new(
    [System.StringComparer]::OrdinalIgnoreCase)

foreach ($file in $resolvedFiles) {
    $content = Get-Content -Path $file.FullName -Raw -Encoding UTF8
    $tables  = Get-TablesFromXmla -Content $content
    $count   = $tables.Count

    Write-Host &quot;  [$($file.Name)] Found $count table(s).&quot; -ForegroundColor Cyan

    foreach ($t in $tables) {
        if (-not $allResults.ContainsKey($t)) {
            $allResults[$t] = [System.Collections.Generic.List[string]]::new()
        }
        [void]$allResults[$t].Add($file.Name)
    }
}

if ($allResults.Count -eq 0) {
    Write-Warning &quot;No Oracle tables found across all input files.&quot;
    exit 1
}

$sortedTables = $allResults.Keys | Sort-Object

# ── Format output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
$lines = [System.Collections.Generic.List[string]]::new()

switch ($Format) {
    &quot;list&quot; {
        if ($WithSource) {
            $lines.Add((&quot;{0,-50}  {1}&quot; -f &quot;TABLE NAME&quot;, &quot;SOURCE FILE(S)&quot;))
            $lines.Add(&quot;-&quot; * 80)
            foreach ($t in $sortedTables) {
                $srcs = ($allResults[$t] | Sort-Object) -join &quot;, &quot;
                $lines.Add((&quot;{0,-50}  {1}&quot; -f $t, $srcs))
            }
        } else {
            $lines.Add(&quot;Oracle Tables Found ($($allResults.Count) total)&quot;)
            $lines.Add(&quot;=&quot; * 50)
            foreach ($t in $sortedTables) {
                $lines.Add(&quot;  $t&quot;)
            }
        }
    }
    &quot;csv&quot; {
        $lines.Add(&quot;table_name,source_file&quot;)
        foreach ($t in $sortedTables) {
            foreach ($src in ($allResults[$t] | Sort-Object)) {
                $lines.Add(&quot;$t,$src&quot;)
            }
        }
    }
    &quot;tsv&quot; {
        $lines.Add(&quot;table_name`tsource_file&quot;)
        foreach ($t in $sortedTables) {
            foreach ($src in ($allResults[$t] | Sort-Object)) {
                $lines.Add(&quot;$t`t$src&quot;)
            }
        }
    }
}

# ── Output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
$outputText = $lines -join &quot;`r`n&quot;

if ($Output) {
    $outputText | Out-File -FilePath $Output -Encoding UTF8
    Write-Host &quot;Results written to: $Output&quot; -ForegroundColor Green
} else {
    Write-Host &quot;&quot;
    Write-Host $outputText
}
</code></pre>

Q: Convert raw SQL with comma-JOINed tables related by identically named columns to CodeIgniter&#39;s query builder A: <p>From the CI docs...</p>

<pre><code>$this-&gt;db-&gt;select('*');
$this-&gt;db-&gt;from('blogs');
$this-&gt;db-&gt;join('comments', 'comments.id = blogs.id');

$query = $this-&gt;db-&gt;get();

// Produces: 
// SELECT * FROM blogs
// JOIN comments ON comments.id = blogs.id
</code></pre>

<p>So in your case, I would not use the cartisian product in your <code>FROM</code>, I would actually use a join.</p>

<pre><code>$this-&gt;db-&gt;select("... your fields here...");
$this-&gt;db-&gt;from("nwsite");
$this-&gt;db-&gt;join("calcdata", "nwsite.siteid = calcdata.siteid");
$this-&gt;db-&gt;where("nwsite.time", "2011-10-29 12:45:00");

$query = $this-&gt;db-&gt;get();
</code></pre>

<p>For Future reference, I often utilize</p>

<pre><code>die($this-&gt;db-&gt;last_query());
</code></pre>

<p>to output the actual query that's being generated.  It makes it easier to debug and compare to what you are attempting to generate.</p>

